From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 18:47:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: add port README with build/deploy/test docs

Validation: not required (documentation-only change).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; drafted the document)

Refuse to deploy onto a vendor OpenHarmony distribution.

deploy.py overwrites libraries in /system, and nothing stopped it from doing so
on a HarmonyOS phone that happened to be the attached device. The shim only
implements the OpenHarmony NWeb ABI and is only ever reached through the SERVO
branch of a patched nweb_helper, so on a vendor distribution -- which ships its
own ArkWeb -- the push cannot select Servo and only risks the device's web stack.

Refuse unless --allow-non-openharmony is given, keyed on
const.product.os.dist.name, which OpenHarmony defines only for distributions
built on top of it (a HarmonyOS device answers "HarmonyOS"; vanilla OpenHarmony
leaves it unset). Deliberately not keyed on const.ohos.fullname: distributions
report the underlying OpenHarmony base there, so a HarmonyOS phone answers
"OpenHarmony-7.0.0.101" and would pass that check.

Validation: Test by running deploy.py --dry-run against a HarmonyOS device (must exit non-zero naming the distribution) and against a vanilla OpenHarmony device such as a DAYU200 (must report "none (vanilla OpenHarmony)" and proceed).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <jschwender@posteo.net>
